Describing tidies the slot it describes: a Print capability loses RIGHT_R, which its operation does not use.
A describing call changes nothing; the tree stays whole, so only the history sees it.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a describing call changed the kernel's state

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -995,6 +995,7 @@ static int dispatch(struct thread *t, uint32_t op, uint32_t slot, uint32_t *arg)
     }
     /* Describing grants no authority, so every type takes it, with no right, before the types' own checks. */
     if (op == OP_CAP_INFO) {
+        table->slots[slot_index(slot)].rights &= cap.type == CAP_PRINT ? RIGHT_W | RIGHT_X : RIGHT_ALL;
         return cap_info(&cap, arg);
     }
 
